export anchor EndCreditsStyle:
    number: 91
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: End credits
    idea: The dashboard rolls like film end credits on a pale screen, everything centred on one axis with italic roles on the left and spaced capital names on the right, and the week's chart mirrored across the same line.
    base: light
    palette:
        screen: #f5f3ee, the page
        tint: #ebe8e1, the focus halo
        ink: #121212, names, rules, this week bars and the primary button
        dim: #5a5752, roles and captions
        smoke: #8e8a83, last week bars, never text
        faint: #d6d2c9, axis lines and meter tracks
        green: #2a6537, On track
        amber: #8a5400, At risk
        red: #9d2020, Behind and overdue
    type:
        Two stacks. Names use Optima, Candara, Noto Sans, Segoe UI, Arial
        in capitals, the greeting 64px at 300 tracked 0.06em, figures 44px
        at 300, project names 19px at 500 tracked 0.14em, block titles
        13px tracked 0.4em, and values 15 to 16px. Roles use Hoefler Text,
        Iowan Old Style, Georgia italic at 16 to 19px in dim grey.
    layout:
        Everything is centred on a single vertical axis with a 980px
        column. The header is a title card, the brand in capitals spaced
        0.5em, a centred nav line, then a centred underlined search, the
        New project button, a round bell and the user in italic. The
        opening reads Brightwork presents, a huge thin capital Good
        morning, Mara and the italic date, then with special attention to
        over a red clock line saying 4 tasks are overdue. Starring lists
        the four numbers as credit pairs, the italic role right aligned to
        the axis and the big figure left aligned. The projects appear as
        six credit blocks in three columns, each a spaced capital name
        over role and value pairs for Team, Progress with a thin meter,
        Tasks, Due and Status. Recent scenes pairs each time with its
        event across the axis. Running time is a mirrored bar chart, last
        week growing left in grey and this week growing right in black,
        with weekday and both dates in the middle. A closing line credits
        the Brightwork team. Below 900px blocks go two across, then one,
        and on a phone the scene pairs stack centred.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 72px between credit blocks, 32px between the role and name columns and 64px between project blocks.
    density: Sparse and slow, read top to bottom like a roll.
    corners: Square. Swatches and the bell are the only circles.
    borders: Almost none. A 48px rule under each block title and 1px underlines on fields.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Thin marks only where they carry meaning. On track is a tick, At
        risk a triangle, Behind double down chevrons and overdue a clock,
        each beside its spaced capital word.
    focus: A 2px ink outline offset 4px with an 8px pale tint halo.
    tone: Credit roll phrasing, such as Brightwork presents, Starring, with special attention to and Running time.
